    "result_text": "All 50 tests pass and the build succeeds. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked household duplicate handling to match the spec. All 50 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n### Changes\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- **Deterministic `householdId`**: Replaced the old address-based, opt-in `assignHousehold`/`householdIdFor` logic with `computeHouseholdId(owner)`, which is now called for **every** owner. It returns the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` (an absent postcode contributes an empty string). Owners sharing last name + postcode converge on the same id automatically, with no cross-owner mutation.\n- **Reordered the create flow** in `addOwner`: compute `householdId` \u2192 `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (exact key, always) \u2192 `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` **only when not** `sharesHousehold` \u2192 `assignPossibleDuplicate`.\n- **New `rejectHouseholdDuplicate`**: rejects (409) when any existing owner already shares the computed `householdId`. `sharesHousehold` now only *bypasses this block* (creating a declared member); it no longer creates the link, and it never bypasses the exact identity-key check.\n- **`assignPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold)`**: a declared household member is no longer flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\n**`HouseholdDuplicateException.java`** (new) + **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`**: dedicated exception mapped to 409.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: updated `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, `identityKey`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions/examples to reflect the deterministic, always-computed behavior.\n\n### Behavior now matching the spec\n- Same last name + postcode \u2192 same `householdId` (Cp11, Cp36), and duplicate detection + identity key key off it (Cp03, Cp25, Cp28).\n- A second owner with the same last name + postcode \u2192 409 household duplicate (Cp10, Cp35), unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member and **not** flagged `possibleDuplicate` (Cp35, Cp23).\n\nNote: there is no household-*size* term in the membership-level computation in this codebase (it derives from email + namesake count, capped at 3), so nothing there needed re-pointing \u2014 Cp23 confirms the third member stays at level 2.",
